From 142e3c96189ff6d0876e5db76181410d353073b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:27:33 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Practice experience: instant start, stage view, cues, keys,
 loop speed-up, recording, my list, room, offline

The engine and instruments preload when the page opens. Tempo, key and
feel are remembered per tune. A quick row above the chart holds You play,
tempo steps, Record and Stage. The count-in is shown large and a cue
announces when the melody leaves or returns. Stage view shows only a
large chart with the current line on top, fullscreen with the screen kept
awake. Keys and page-turner pedals drive the transport and tempo. Loops
can speed up each pass. Takes record the band with the microphone,
aligned by output latency. Starred tunes form a list that can play in
order. A small-room reverb, a speaker-delay setting and pause on audio
interruptions are added. A manifest and service worker make the app
installable and usable offline. feature-test.cjs covers these in Chromium.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01MFtnqVmArJUVScHreHoD7y
